  <!-- ============ BEFORE YOU START ============ -->
  <section class="chapter intro-note" id="hello">
    <div class="chapter-label">Before You Start</div>
    <h2>A Quick Word, Then We Get to Work</h2>
    <p>You already know me from the Playbook, so I'll skip the life story. The part that matters for this: I've reinvented myself more than once. Foundry worker, then 17-year draftsman, now a guy who gets paid on his own terms. None of those turns followed a tidy formula. They came from years of research, trial and error, and a pile of dead ends. Most of it long before AI was even around to help. This workbook is the culmination of what I learned the hard way, boiled down to a handful of thought exercises. AI just does the part it's actually good at: speeds up the thinking. (One of these prompts is the one a reader told me "may have saved my career.")</p>
    <p><strong>One bias I should name.</strong> I'm not chasing the biggest thing. I'm building the <em>calmest</em> thing that still pays well, and I'll be nudging you the same way. That comes from a book, <em>Company of One</em> by Paul Jarvis. A few years back it stopped being something I read and became my operating system. Success is more <em>freedom</em>, not more growth. Design the life first, then build the business that funds it. Small, owned, and profitable beats big and panicking.</p>
    <p>So when this workbook keeps steering you toward something AI-proof, something you own, and something you'd do anyway, that's the lens. If your dream is to build an empire and sell it for millions, this can still help. Just filter my advice accordingly.</p>

    <p>Two things, so you get your money's worth:</p>
    <ul class="case-list">
      <li><strong>Actually do it.</strong> Reading won't move you. Filling in the box, running the prompts, and writing your North Star will. Block off an hour and a free AI account, and you'll walk out with it done.</li>
      <li><strong>Be honest in the inputs.</strong> The AI is only as sharp as what you feed it. Rough and real beats polished and vague every time.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>And my promise: do the work, and if you don't walk away with a direction worth building toward, email me at <strong>coreysretirement@fastmail.com</strong> and I'll refund every penny. No questions, no hard feelings. The risk's on me.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ HOW THIS WORKS ============ -->
  <section class="chapter how" id="how">
    <div class="chapter-label">How This Works</div>
    <h2>Fill It In Once. The Whole Thing Builds Itself.</h2>
    <p>Every module has a short read, a quick exercise, and a copy-paste AI prompt. You'll fill in your raw materials <em>one time</em> in the box below (your age, your roles, your skills, the rest), and it drops into every prompt automatically. No retyping. No digging.</p>
    <p>For each prompt, hit <strong>Copy</strong>, paste it into ChatGPT, Claude, or Gemini (a free account is fine), and answer what it asks. The outputs stack, module by module, into one finished <strong>"My North Star"</strong> page at the end. You leave holding a document, not a vibe.</p>
    <p class="meta-line"><strong>What you need:</strong> a free AI account and about 45–60 minutes. <strong>What you walk away with:</strong> a named, AI-proof direction and your first move, done in one sitting.</p>

